  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Commerce obligated $125M on contracts in FY2027 to date. The FY2027 to date total reflects 418 awards and an average award size of $300K. Obligations fell 97.5% year over year. The FY2027 to date level is small compared with recent full fiscal years: FY22 was $4.1B, FY23 was $5B, FY24 was $5.2B, FY25 was $4.2B, and FY26 was $5.1B. Contracting in FY2027 to date is concentrated in IT and professional services. Other Computer Related Services accounted for $68.9M and Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $39.4M, together representing the bulk of FY2027 to date obligations. General Dynamics Information Technology, Inc. is the top vendor in FY2027 to date with $61M in obligations. The remainder of the top vendor list includes large professional services and technology firms with obligations ranging from $12.3M down to $1.8M. The data are fiscal year to date and represent obligations, not final fiscal year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Commerce's contract spending changed year over year?",
        "body": "The Department of Commerce obligated $125M in FY2027 to date, down 97.5% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations before FY2027 were $4.1B in FY22, $5B in FY23, $5.2B in FY24, $4.2B in FY25, and $5.1B in FY26. The current-year total is partial for the fiscal year to date and reflects lower obligations so far."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the dominant categories and vendors so far in FY2027?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is the largest category with $68.9M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services with $39.4M. General Dynamics Information Technology, Inc. is the largest vendor with $61M, and ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC is second with $12.3M. The top ten categories and vendors show concentration in IT and professional services."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Commerce spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Commerce has obligated $125M on contracts in FY2027 to date. The FY2027 to date totals reflect 418 awards and an average award size of $300K, and obligations fell 97.5% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Commerce buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Commerce buys mainly IT and professional services in FY2027 to date. Other Computer Related Services accounted for $68.9M and Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $39.4M, with Engineering Services at $4.2M and other categories ranging down to $1.1M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Commerce's largest contractors?",
      "a": "The largest contractors to the Department of Commerce in FY2027 to date are GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. with $61M and ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC with $12.3M. Other top vendors include HALVIK LLC with $9.6M, BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC with $9.2M, and SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION with $7.8M."
